# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.net26, REST=1 (with WIFID=1), MORE_JOBS="com.apple.bluetoothd com.apple.BlueTool",
# NILINJECT=Preferences, connsys_step=17, XNU_SECS=150, applog=1 applog_name=Preferences.
#
# What run 94 (logs/lancelot-connsys46.log) said: the dictionary that killed Settings is a settings
# row -- keys label, cell, bundle, iconImage, isController, id, restrictByID -- and iconImage is nil:
# a pane's icon that its own bundle does not carry where iOS 16 looks for it. With that pair left out,
# Settings opens and stays 8.8 s, then dies without a word (the kernel only says "Corpse allowed 1 of
# 5", and no line of the program's standard error comes before it).
#
# So the same library now catches the signals too (SIGTRAP, SIGABRT, SIGILL, SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGSYS),
# says which one, with its address, and names every frame as image + offset through dladdr -- that way
# the private frameworks that are not in the shared cache (the frames of run 94 at 0x23c1d1f78, above
# the cache's 0x200000000) get a name as well. "end" on the watchdie line keeps the tail.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 22
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 10
/redwood/bin/net_test fbwait 60
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 16
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.543 0.712
/redwood/bin/net_test watchdie Preferences 30 end